{"type":"message","id":"c3ab5172","parentId":"0b4f86f4","timestamp":"2026-05-23T18:05:02.751Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST /send endpoint is returning error code 1101. This might be a Cloudflare error (1101 = \"Worker threw exception\" or similar). The GET endpoints work fine with X-API-Key header but POST doesn't work with the same auth method.\n\nLet me try a few more variations to see if maybe the body format is different or if there's a different endpoint structure.\n\nActually wait - maybe the issue is that the platform expects the API key to be passed in a different way for POST requests. Or perhaps there's a rate limit or the worker is malfunctioning for POST.\n\nLet me check if maybe the body is being rejected due to some validation. Maybe the content field is too long or contains special characters. Let me try with a much simpler payload.\n","thinkingSignature":"6dd3c819c108425a3bd7d0a2dbab61a4e65222601347a64a915343e62cdf0299"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0mv3c27r5qh5_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"content\":\"heartbeat test\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":130,"output":246,"cacheRead":22280,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22656,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779559487912,"responseId":"06611f4012895eb8977d5f388495db6b"}}
